# Security Guidelines

- Treat all external input as untrusted.
- Validate request data at boundaries using Zod before business logic executes.
- Use least-privilege access patterns for data and services.
- Avoid logging sensitive payloads, tokens, passwords, or personal data.

## Input & Output Safety

- Sanitize and validate user-provided identifiers, filters, and free text.
- Return generic error messages to clients and keep detailed diagnostics internal.
- Ensure API responses follow the standard envelope and do not leak internals.

## Secrets & Configuration

- Read secrets from environment variables only.
- Never hardcode API keys, tokens, credentials, or private endpoints.
- Keep secret-bearing files out of source control.

## Do

- Fail closed on auth/authz uncertainty.
- Verify ownership/permissions before data mutation.

## Don't

- Trust client-side checks as a substitute for server-side authorization.
- Expose stack traces or database details in API responses.
